# Solace-AI Docker build-context excludes.
# All service Dockerfiles build from the repository ROOT (`context: .`), so this single
# .dockerignore governs EVERY image build.
#
# SECURITY (Phase C P2-15): never bake secrets into an image layer. The working-tree .env
# holds live third-party API keys and must NOT enter any build context. .env.prod (prod
# secrets) is injected at runtime via `env_file:`, never at build time, so it is excluded too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS / tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# Python caches / build artifacts (never needed at build; keeps context small)
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
**/coverage.xml
htmlcov

# Virtualenvs / local dev
.venv
venv
env
node_modules

# Logs / scratch
*.log
tests/logs
**/tests/
tests/
src/models/
docs/
infrastructure/aws-staging/
**/logs/
.secrets
secrets
# D-07 (SOPS + age): images never carry even the encrypted files (render_secrets.py runs on the host), nor age keys
deploy/secrets
**/*.agekey
**/keys.txt
# Docker matches these case-sensitively, but git on the Windows host ignores case (core.ignorecase=true) and so
# hides case variants from scripts/ci/secret_scan.py; the classes keep every letter case out of the context.
# key.txt is age-keygen's documented default name; *.key is gitignored too.
[dD][eE][pP][lL][oO][yY]/[sS][eE][cC][rR][eE][tT][sS]
**/*.[aA][gG][eE][kK][eE][yY]
**/[kK][eE][yY][sS].[tT][xX][tT]
**/[kK][eE][yY].[tT][xX][tT]
**/*.[kK][eE][yY]
